target: Plan B's child exits when it cannot run the restart script

opensync-rpi / opensync-lab: target_managers_restart() closes every descriptor
from 3 up (the manager's libev epoll descriptor too), forks, and the child execs
<scripts dir>/restart.sh. When that exec fails, the function logged "Failed to
execute plan B!" and returned: the child ran on in the inherited event loop,
epoll_wait() failed with EINVAL on the reused descriptor and libev aborted --
a core at every Plan B. In the pods the exec always fails: their scripts dir
is /usr/opensync/scripts (where opensync.init lives), and core's SYSTEMD rootfs
installs restart.sh in /usr/opensync/bin. Seen as an sm core at every general
restart (SM's OVSDB library calls Plan B when ovsdb-server goes away). The child
now exits; the restart itself is systemd's (opensync.service Restart=on-failure
in the pod image).

Upstream: the return after a failed exec is an OpenSync core bug as released in
6.6.1.0: target_managers_restart() in src/lib/target/src/target_stub.c (the stub
every target without IMPL_target_managers_restart uses). Why the exec fails in
these pods is ours: their CONFIG_TARGET_PATH_SCRIPTS (/usr/opensync/scripts, for
opensync.init) is not where core's SYSTEMD rootfs installs restart.sh (bin/), and
core's opensync.service has Restart=no. Not reported (the owner decides).

diff --git a/src/lib/target/src/target_stub.c b/src/lib/target/src/target_stub.c
index f802a4b2..76a71e3e 100644
--- a/src/lib/target/src/target_stub.c
+++ b/src/lib/target/src/target_stub.c
@@ -391,6 +391,12 @@ void target_managers_restart(void)
     execl(cmd, cmd, NULL);
 
     LOG(EMERG, "Failed to execute plan B!");
+    /*
+     * Never return to the caller: this child runs on in the parent's event loop,
+     * whose descriptors were closed above, and libev aborts in it
+     * (epoll_wait: Invalid argument) -- a core at every Plan B.
+     */
+    _exit(1);
 }
 #endif
 
